      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "content": "1. Background: Why Europeans Came to India"
    },
    {
      "type": "keyFacts",
      "title": "Key Takeaways",
      "items": [
        "Europeans sought a direct sea route to India to control the lucrative spice trade and bypass overland monopoly.",
        "The Portuguese were the first European nation to establish trade settlements and maritime hegemony in India.",
        "The Dutch, English, and French established rival trading companies throughout the 17th century.",
        "The Anglo-French Rivalry culminated in the Carnatic Wars, cementing British dominance over India."
      ],
      "id": "2vdnsx9"
